{"title":"Career Roadmap · Perfusionist","role":"Perfusionist","summary":"A Perfusionist is a specialized cardiovascular healthcare professional who operates and manages cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) and extracorporeal circulation systems during cardiac and selected major surgical procedures.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Perfusion Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Perfusionist is a specialized cardiovascular healthcare professional who operates and manages cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) and extracorporeal circulation systems during cardiac and selected major surgical procedures."},{"type":"p","text":"The perfusionist works closely with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiothoracic surgeons"},{"text":"Cardiac anaesthesiologists"},{"text":"Cardiologists"},{"text":"Critical-care teams"},{"text":"Operating-room staff"},{"text":"Cardiovascular technologists"},{"text":"Nurses"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Core responsibilities can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiopulmonary bypass"},{"text":"Oxygenation and ventilation support through extracorporeal circuits"},{"text":"Blood-flow management"},{"text":"Temperature management"},{"text":"Anticoagulation monitoring according to institutional protocols"},{"text":"Blood conservation"},{"text":"Extracorporeal circuit preparation"},{"text":"Cell-salvage systems"},{"text":"ECMO support where appropriately trained"},{"text":"Emergency extracorporeal support"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Because perfusion is a high-risk, highly specialized clinical profession, the exact scope, registration requirements, and permitted responsibilities depend on the jurisdiction, qualification, hospital and applicable professional regulations."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc / B.Voc / Degree in Perfusion Technology","Clinical Training / Internship","Cardiac Surgery & CPB Exposure","Junior Perfusionist","Perfusionist","Senior Perfusionist","ECMO / Advanced Perfusion Specialist","Chief Perfusionist / Perfusion Services Lead","Clinical Educator / Researcher / Perfusion Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"For this role, hands-on supervised clinical training in cardiopulmonary bypass is essential."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"UG Years 1–2"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, cardiovascular and respiratory sciences"}],[{"text":"UG Years 3–4"},{"text":"Perfusion equipment, CPB, blood management and cardiac surgery"}],[{"text":"Clinical Internship"},{"text":"Supervised perfusion procedures and operating-room exposure"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Routine CPB procedures and equipment management"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Complex cardiac cases and advanced extracorporeal support"}],[{"text":"Senior Career"},{"text":"ECMO, quality management, leadership and education"}],[{"text":"Advanced Career"},{"text":"Perfusion services management, research or specialist practice"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Biomedical Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic Focus"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pharmacology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Essential Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Build particularly strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiovascular system"},{"text":"Respiratory system"},{"text":"Renal system"},{"text":"Nervous system"},{"text":"Blood and coagulation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiac cycle"},{"text":"Cardiac output"},{"text":"Blood pressure"},{"text":"Oxygen tran