ation"},{"text":"Emergency management"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Patient safety"},{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"Quality improvement"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Perfusion Technology graduate should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced cardiovascular and respiratory physiology"},{"text":"Strong understanding of CPB"},{"text":"Supervised experience with heart-lung machines"},{"text":"Knowledge of oxygenators and perfusion circuits"},{"text":"Blood-gas interpretation skills"},{"text":"Anticoagulation knowledge"},{"text":"Cardioplegia fundamentals"},{"text":"Blood-conservation knowledge"},{"text":"Perfusion emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Cardiac-surgery operating-room exposure"},{"text":"ICU experience"},{"text":"ECMO fundamentals"},{"text":"Strong documentation and communication"},{"text":"BLS/emergency training"},{"text":"Understanding of professional scope and patient-safety protocols"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Perfusion Technology","Cardiovascular & Respiratory Physiology","Cardiopulmonary Bypass","Perfusion Monitoring","Cardiac Surgery","Advanced Perfusion","ECMO / Specialized Perfusion"]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest professional positioning is:"},{"type":"p","text":"A highly specialized cardiovascular technology professional capable of safely supporting extracorporeal circulation during cardiac surgery, with strong expertise in cardiopulmonary bypass, perfusion monitoring, oxygenation, blood management, temperature control, emergency preparedness and advanced extracorporeal technologies such as ECMO."}]}]}